{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q331002","formula":"BrCs","hill":"BrCs","elements":["Br","Cs"],"composition":{"Br":1.0,"Cs":1.0},"names":{"en":"Cesium bromide","ru":"Бромид цезия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Caesium bromide or cesium bromide is an ionic compound of caesium and bromine with the chemical formula CsBr. It is a white or transparent solid with melting point at 636 °C that readily dissolves in water. Its bulk crystals have the cubic CsCl structure, but the structure changes to the rocksalt type in nanometer-thin film grown on mica, LiF, KBr or NaCl substrates.","ru":"Броми́д це́зия (цезий бромистый) — CsBr, неорганическое бинарное соединение цезия и брома, цезиевая соль бромоводородной кислоты. Бесцветное (в кристаллическом виде) вещество с ионной структурой; нелетучее, термически устойчивое, хорошо растворимое в воде. Кристаллическая решётка CsBr — кубическая примитивная типа CsCl."},"fame":29,"pubchemCid":24592,"mass":212.81,"charge":0,"smiles":"[Br-].[Cs+]","inchikey":"LYQFWZFBNBDLEO-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"cesium bromide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-22906","atoms":9,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.326,0.0,0.0],[0.0,4.326,0.0],[0.0,0.0,4.326]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Cs"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":4.326,"el":"Cs"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.326,"z":0.0,"el":"Cs"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.326,"z":4.326,"el":"Cs"},{"x":4.326,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Cs"},{"x":4.326,"y":0.0,"z":4.326,"el":"Cs"},{"x":4.326,"y":4.326,"z":0.0,"el":"Cs"},{"x":4.326,"y":4.326,"z":4.326,"el":"Cs"},{"x":2.163,"y":2.163,"z":2.163,"el":"Br"}],"bonds":[[0,8,1],[1,8,1],[2,8,1],[3,8,1],[4,8,1],[5,8,1],[6,8,1],[7,8,1]],"cellOrigin":[0,0,0]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q331002","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","n